Z||000012||rockcrawl||02-05-2001||08:52 PM||||Josh,<BR> From the toolbar at the top, select Image/Adjust/Replace Color. Use the eye dropper on the picture to select the color you want to replace. the + adds more pixel colors and the - removes a selected pixel color. Adjust the Hue, Saturation, and Lightness to your liking (the Hue is what changes the color). If the background is also changing and you don't want it to, you can select just the parts you want to change and then click the 'selection' button on the replace color table. Play with it for a while and you'll get the hang of it. <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
